{title: 632 - Until Then}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #632 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 632}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]My [Eb/Bb]heart [Dm/A]can [Bb]sing when I pause [Eb/Bb]to [Bb]remember,
[Adim]A heartache [F]here is but [Eb/Bb]a [Dm/A]stepping stone.
[Dm/A]Along a [Bb]trail, that's winding [Adim]always [Eb/Bb]upward,
[Eb]This [F7/Eb]troubled [Eb/Bb]world, [Bb]is not my final [F]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb/D]But until then, [Adim]my [Dm/A]heart will [Bb]go [F7/A]on [Bb]singing,
[Bb]Until [Adim]then, with joy I'll [Gm]carry [Adim]on,
[Bb]Until the [Cm]day [Bm]my [B]eyes [Cm]behold [Eb/Bb]the [Gm]city,
[Bb]Until [Dm/A]the day [Adim]God calls [Bb]me home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]The [Eb/Bb]things [Dm/A]of [Bb]earth will dim and [Eb/Bb]loose [Bb]there [Dm/A]value,
[Adim]If we recall [F]they're borrowed [Eb/Bb]for [Dm/A]awhile;
[Dm/A]And [Eb/Bb]things [Dm/A]of [Bb]earth that cause the [Adim]heart [Bb]to [Eb/Bb]tremble,
[Eb]Remember there, [Bb]will only bring [Adim]a [F]smile.
{end_of_verse}
